"spiders.Spider.from_crawler` method was called to generate a new instance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:463
msgid ""
"Non-default values for the :setting:`SCHEDULER_PRIORITY_QUEUE` setting may "
"stop working. Scheduler priority queue classes now need to handle :class:"
"`~scrapy.Request` objects instead of arbitrary Python data structures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:468
msgid ""
"An additional ``crawler`` parameter has been added to the ``__init__`` "
"method of the :class:`~scrapy.core.scheduler.Scheduler` class. Custom "
"scheduler subclasses which don't accept arbitrary parameters in their "
"``__init__`` method might break because of this change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:473
msgid "For more information, see :setting:`SCHEDULER`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:475
msgid "See also :ref:`1.7-deprecation-removals` below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:481
msgid ""
"A new scheduler priority queue, ``scrapy.pqueues."
"DownloaderAwarePriorityQueue``, may be :ref:`enabled <broad-crawls-scheduler-"
"priority-queue>` for a significant scheduling improvement on crawls "
"targeting multiple web domains, at the cost of no "
"``CONCURRENT_REQUESTS_PER_IP`` support (:gh:`3520`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:487
msgid ""
"A new :attr:`.Request.cb_kwargs` attribute provides a cleaner way to pass "
"keyword arguments to callback methods (:gh:`1138`, :gh:`3563`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:491
msgid ""
"A new :class:`JSONRequest <scrapy.http.JsonRequest>` class offers a more "
"convenient way to build JSON requests (:gh:`3504`, :gh:`3505`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:494
msgid ""
"A ``process_request`` callback passed to the :class:`~scrapy.spiders.Rule` "
"``__init__`` method now receives the :class:`~scrapy.http.Response` object "
"that originated the request as its second argument (:gh:`3682`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:498
msgid ""
"A new ``restrict_text`` parameter for the :attr:`LinkExtractor <scrapy."
"linkextractors.lxmlhtml.LxmlLinkExtractor>` ``__init__`` method allows "
"filtering links by linking text (:gh:`3622`, :gh:`3635`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:503
msgid ""
"A new :setting:`FEED_STORAGE_S3_ACL` setting allows defining a custom ACL "
"for feeds exported to Amazon S3 (:gh:`3607`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:506
msgid ""
"A new :setting:`FEED_STORAGE_FTP_ACTIVE` setting allows using FTP’s active "
"connection mode for feeds exported to FTP servers (:gh:`3829`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:509
msgid ""
"A new :setting:`METAREFRESH_IGNORE_TAGS` setting allows overriding which "
"HTML tags are ignored when searching a response for HTML meta tags that "
"trigger a redirect (:gh:`1422`, :gh:`3768`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:513
msgid ""
"A new :reqmeta:`redirect_reasons` request meta key exposes the reason "
"(status code, meta refresh) behind every followed redirect (:gh:`3581`, :gh:"
"`3687`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:517
msgid ""
"The ``SCRAPY_CHECK`` variable is now set to the ``true`` string during runs "
