#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:1376
msgid ""
"This release comes rather soon after 1.2.2 for one main reason: it was found "
"out that releases since 0.18 up to 1.2.2 (included) use some backported code "
"from Twisted (``scrapy.xlib.tx.*``), even if newer Twisted modules are "
"available. Scrapy now uses ``twisted.web.client`` and ``twisted.internet."
"endpoints`` directly. (See also cleanups below.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:1383
msgid ""
"As it is a major change, we wanted to get the bug fix out quickly while not "
"breaking any projects using the 1.2 series."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:1389
msgid ""
"``MailSender`` now accepts single strings as values for ``to`` and ``cc`` "
"arguments (:gh:`2272`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:1391
msgid ""
"``scrapy fetch url``, ``scrapy shell url`` and ``fetch(url)`` inside Scrapy "
"shell now follow HTTP redirections by default (:gh:`2290`); See :command:"
"`fetch` and :command:`shell` for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:1394
msgid ""
"``HttpErrorMiddleware`` now logs errors with ``INFO`` level instead of "
"``DEBUG``; this is technically **backward incompatible** so please check "
"your log parsers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../news/1.x.rst:1396
msgid ""
"By default, logger names now use a long-form path, e.g. ``[scrapy.extensions."
"logstats]``, instead of the shorter \"top-level\" variant of prior releases "
"(e.g. ``[scrapy]``); this is **backward incompatible** if you have log "
"parsers expecting the short logger name part. You can switch back to short "
"logger names using :setting:`LOG_SHORT_NAMES` set to ``True``."
msgstr ""

